# {{ customer }} — {{ solution }} Sources

## Purpose

Define the real systems and providers outside the principal solution boundary that originate or externally curate data.

## Boundary Rules

Include operational systems, partner platforms, authoritative external datasets, and external providers. Exclude staging, queues, transit buckets, internal warehouse schemas, file formats, and downstream delivery products.

## Source Classification

| Classification | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Operational system | Supports a business process and originates operational records. |
| Finance system | Originates financial commitments, payments, or ledger records. |
| Partner or council source | Externally managed organisational source. |
| External dataset or provider | Curates reference, classification, or outcome information. |
| Legacy source | Retained for historical or transitional data. |

